WEBVTT

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:13.490
Morning, Chisame-chan.

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:20.870
It's finally time, huh?

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:26.710
What's with the ribbons?

00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:29.590
They're headbands we got at cram school.

00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:32.600
Unlike you, I'm ranked B,

00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:34.970
so I gotta rely on luck.

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:54.240
この坂を上り切ったら
kono saka o noborikittara

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:58.200
必ず見える景色が好きだって
kanarazu mieru keshiki ga suki datte

00:00:58.200 --> 00:00:58.240
必ず見える景色が好きだって

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:04.370
背中に羽を持つあの子も言って笑ってた
senaka ni hane o motsu ano ko mo itte waratteta

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:08.040
ドキドキが一瞬で
dokidoki ga isshun de

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:12.130
トキメキになっていくんだなんて
tokimeki ni natteikunda nante

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:15.840
あの頃は信じられなくて
ano koro wa shinjirarenakute

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:20.810
ただ見惚れていたよ
tada mitoreteita yo

00:01:21.260 --> 00:01:25.440
このスピードに乗せた体温が
kono supiido ni noseta taion ga

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:29.190
今全身で伝う　通じ合う
ima zenshin de tsutau tsuujiau

00:01:29.190 --> 00:01:32.820
物語の鍵はこの手に
monogatari no kagi wa kono te ni

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:36.320
ぎゅっと強く握っているから
gyutto tsuyoku nigitteiru kara

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:40.030
感じて　応えて　風になる
kanjite kotaete kaze ni naru

00:01:40.030 --> 00:01:43.700
空に溶けて海を抱きしめる
sora ni tokete umi o dakishimeru

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:47.620
新しい世界が見えるはず
atarashii sekai ga mieru hazu

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:54.710
さぁ確かめに行ってみよう
saa tashikame ni ittemiyou

00:02:04.970 --> 00:02:05.770
New Students!!
Episode 9

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:08.480
Goooood Morning!
New Students!!
Episode 9

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:08.940
Everyone, please do your best today!
New Students!!
Episode 9

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:11.560
Everyone, please do your best today!

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:13.150
What's she doing?

00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:16.490
She's supposed to be a guide, or so I've heard.

00:02:16.490 --> 00:02:19.740
Oh wait, come to think of it, I think
Onee-chan said she'd be a guide, too.

00:02:20.030 --> 00:02:23.330
And once you've passed your exams,

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:26.080
don't forget to come visit the Bike Club!

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:27.540
Don't forget!

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:30.120
Vrooom vroom vroooom!

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:31.580
What the...

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:33.920
Hey, it's Yume!

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:35.630
Hey!

00:02:35.630 --> 00:02:38.260
Vrooom! Drrrr!

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:40.430
That's my sister.

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:48.560
She's from my class, Nakano Chisame-san.

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:52.190
You've been on the circuit
ever since middle school, right?

00:02:52.190 --> 00:02:54.690
No, since elementary school.

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:58.950
My! You started being a renegade that young?

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:00.950
What a promising junior!

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:05.410
How about it? Join the Bike Club and
let's experience the wind and freedom!

00:03:05.410 --> 00:03:08.080
I haven't even passed the exam yet.

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:09.660
I'm ranked B, after all.

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:13.040
V-Vrooom? D-Drrrr

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:14.880
vroooom vroom vrooom vroooom!

00:03:15.170 --> 00:03:17.510
Onee-chan, what are you doing?

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:22.970
She's subliminally giving the
message for the Bike Club via engine noises.

00:03:26.350 --> 00:03:28.390
Good luck!

00:03:28.390 --> 00:03:30.270
Drrrrrrrrrrr!

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:33.560
Is your sister sick?

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:34.900
With what?

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:38.070
Okay, begin.

00:03:40.610 --> 00:03:41.900
Alright, I can do this.

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:46.490
I studied all summer to
be able to get into the circuit.

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:50.080
Drrrrrrrr!

00:03:51.210 --> 00:03:51.830
<b>I   English</b>

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:55.330
Why am I remembering
that in the middle of my exam?
<b>I   English</b>

00:03:55.330 --> 00:04:00.050
I didn't choose this school
just because of its bike rules.

00:04:00.050 --> 00:04:04.390
I don't even have a
reason to ride on real roads.

00:04:04.390 --> 00:04:06.930
The circuit is my battleground.

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:10.850
Even back then I was always small,
and was always last in races.

00:04:11.770 --> 00:04:13.520
I was bad at ball sports.

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:16.230
I even ate slowly.

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:19.900
They called me "Little Chisame."

00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:24.360
There isn't a good thing about being small.

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:25.070
Except

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:28.410
when it came to biking.

00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:31.830
Less weight was an advantage.

00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:34.750
I won a minibike race.

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:36.460
I was happy.

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:39.800
What I hated the most about
myself was actually my greatest asset!

00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:46.390
Faster! Even faster!

00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:49.560
In a circuit, I'm unbeatable.

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:53.480
No matter the weather, it's my day!

00:04:56.350 --> 00:05:00.020
Dad bought a new bike.

00:05:00.020 --> 00:05:01.860
When I get my license,

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:04.610
I'll ride a bike like this.

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:08.240
Or not.

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:12.080
In a race, my feet don't need to touch the ground.

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:15.410
But on the real roads,

00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:17.790
you need to stop at these "traffic lights."

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:22.960
I thought my small body was my greatest asset,

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:24.880
but it really is my enemy.

00:05:26.050 --> 00:05:29.800
I never grew taller, and so I had to avoid

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:33.100
the thousands of traffic lights across the country.

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:36.850
In the end, for me, bikes are...

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:40.820
Time's up.

00:05:41.320 --> 00:05:44.490
If I fail, I'm blaming it on that Bike Club!

00:05:44.860 --> 00:05:46.740
How was it, Chisame-chan?

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:49.280
I did what I could.

00:05:50.700 --> 00:05:51.620
What's that?

00:05:55.580 --> 00:05:57.620
Again with that Bike Club.

00:05:59.250 --> 00:06:01.540
You've all seen an off-road bike

00:06:01.540 --> 00:06:05.010
popping wheelies at traffic
lights, haven't you?

00:06:05.010 --> 00:06:08.130
An off-roader <i>must</i> do that, or she'll die.

00:06:08.130 --> 00:06:10.050
What? Is that true?

00:06:10.050 --> 00:06:11.470
I didn't even know.

00:06:11.470 --> 00:06:14.770
You girls sure do listen!

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:15.730
How about it?

00:06:15.730 --> 00:06:18.560
Aren't you getting interested in biking?

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:20.060
Not exactly interested, but...

00:06:20.060 --> 00:06:23.270
I couldn't get that "vroom vroom"
voice from this morning

00:06:23.270 --> 00:06:25.190
out of my head during the exam.

00:06:25.190 --> 00:06:27.900
Me neither.

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:30.360
There were more victims.

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:33.580
Now then, since your exams are over

00:06:33.580 --> 00:06:36.700
let's take some time to talk about bikes!

00:06:36.700 --> 00:06:39.080
We have also prepared some delicious tea.

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:42.380
But if you want to lose weight,
bicycles are better than motorbikes.

00:06:44.550 --> 00:06:46.960
Look! There's someone on a bicycle over there!

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:49.630
She must be from the Bicycle Club.

00:06:49.630 --> 00:06:50.130
Huh?

00:06:50.130 --> 00:06:52.260
May we speak with you?

00:06:52.260 --> 00:06:54.060
Over some tea, perhaps?

00:06:54.060 --> 00:06:56.140
Huh? What?

00:07:00.100 --> 00:07:01.850
Wait, Chisame-chan.

00:07:01.850 --> 00:07:03.480
What's up with her?

00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:06.070
She scared off all the people we attracted.

00:07:11.820 --> 00:07:14.990
Oh I see, Yume-chan passed the exam?

00:07:14.990 --> 00:07:16.740
She did.

00:07:16.740 --> 00:07:19.870
I'm happy knowing my little
sister will be in the same school as me!

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:22.790
And it's already been a
year since you got your license.

00:07:22.790 --> 00:07:25.420
Starting this spring you're gonna
have to share the same bike, right?

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:27.880
Well, about that...

00:07:28.210 --> 00:07:30.260
I'm alright with just a bicycle.

00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:33.430
I was looking forward to riding together.

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:36.140
I guess she just doesn't want to ride one, huh?

00:07:36.560 --> 00:07:38.930
Also, that other girl passed too.

00:07:38.930 --> 00:07:41.440
The one we met during exams.
She had her hair like this.

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:43.060
Oh, her?

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:46.110
But that means we're gonna
be second-years already.

00:07:46.110 --> 00:07:49.280
But, while Spring is for meeting new people,

00:07:49.280 --> 00:07:51.400
you almost leave old friends behind.

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:54.200
Parting? You mean graduation?

00:07:55.780 --> 00:07:56.870
Raimu-senpai!

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:07.460
Raimu-senpai's a third-year.

00:08:07.710 --> 00:08:11.260
I always thought she'd stay
in the club for some reason.

00:08:11.260 --> 00:08:13.010
Obviously not.

00:08:13.010 --> 00:08:15.220
I always thought she was weird,

00:08:15.220 --> 00:08:18.100
but now that she's going to
graduate, I'm kinda sad.

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:21.270
Plus she did all my oil changes.

00:08:21.640 --> 00:08:24.730
And even without telling us,
she cleaned our bikes.

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:29.110
We're probably going to have to
learn to do all of that stuff now.

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:31.280
We should throw a party.

00:08:31.610 --> 00:08:32.860
A party?

00:08:32.860 --> 00:08:34.490
What? That came out of nowhere.

00:08:34.490 --> 00:08:38.950
We should celebrate Raimu-senpai's
graduation with a party in her honor!

00:08:39.370 --> 00:08:42.370
Well, keep it a secret from her.

00:08:42.370 --> 00:08:44.670
Yeah, it'd be fun to surprise her.

00:08:44.670 --> 00:08:47.670
A-All right, I guess.

00:08:47.670 --> 00:08:49.500
I understand.

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:49.840
However, in order to give her a proper graduation,
I understand.

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:52.260
However, in order to give her a proper graduation,

00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:54.630
there are a number of things we must do.

00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:56.010
What would that be?

00:08:56.010 --> 00:09:00.100
We must prove that we can take
care of our bikes without her.

00:09:00.100 --> 00:09:03.140
Oh I see, we should give her peace of mind.

00:09:03.140 --> 00:09:04.640
But how?

00:09:04.890 --> 00:09:07.810
About that, I actually have some ideas.

00:09:11.780 --> 00:09:14.450
Graduation

00:09:15.820 --> 00:09:19.910
Congratulations on your graduation, Senpai!

00:09:33.050 --> 00:09:35.340
Yes, principal's office.

00:09:36.510 --> 00:09:39.970
No way! Akina? It's been so long!

00:09:39.970 --> 00:09:43.390
Ever since that reunion way back.

00:09:43.390 --> 00:09:45.230
Have you been well, Tazuko?

00:09:45.230 --> 00:09:46.310
Yes.

00:09:46.310 --> 00:09:49.270
But why are you calling all of a sudden?

00:09:49.270 --> 00:09:53.650
Well, my daughter's entering
Okanoue in the spring.

00:09:53.650 --> 00:09:54.780
Oh, really?

00:09:54.780 --> 00:09:58.030
Your daughter's coming to our high school, huh?

00:09:59.780 --> 00:10:03.200
Wait, when did you get married?!

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:03.830
<b>Seki Atsuko</b>

00:10:03.830 --> 00:10:04.540
<b>Aratani Yuko</b>

00:10:04.540 --> 00:10:06.750
<b>Nakano Chisame</b>

00:10:06.750 --> 00:10:09.500
Nakano Chisame.

00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:13.000
I never would have thought
you had a child that old.

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:15.840
It's not like I was trying to hide it,

00:10:15.840 --> 00:10:17.930
but I just couldn't bring it up.

00:10:17.930 --> 00:10:22.810
<b>Nakano
You know, you've always tended to avoid men.</b>

00:10:22.810 --> 00:10:24.390
Is that because
<b>Nakano</b>

00:10:24.770 --> 00:10:26.930
of Raimu-senpai?

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:33.520
Please, go out with me.

00:10:33.520 --> 00:10:37.610
It was love at first sight when
I saw you in your leathers.

00:10:37.610 --> 00:10:40.240
Let's start as pager buddies.

00:10:41.780 --> 00:10:44.540
You know, you ride an NSR,

00:10:44.540 --> 00:10:46.660
and I ride its predecessor, the MVX.

00:10:46.660 --> 00:10:49.920
Oh, yeah! I have a gift for you.

00:10:55.090 --> 00:10:56.760
Don't tell me...

00:10:58.420 --> 00:11:02.300
Is that the legendary
silencer-shaped container?

00:11:02.550 --> 00:11:04.470
Have a coffee.

00:11:04.850 --> 00:11:06.970
L-Lame.

00:11:08.350 --> 00:11:10.060
Well...

00:11:10.060 --> 00:11:13.650
If you win a bike race,
I wouldn't mind going out with you.

00:11:14.150 --> 00:11:17.110
But you're going up against

00:11:17.440 --> 00:11:20.610
that Kawasaki Mach, and Raimu-senpai.

00:11:22.070 --> 00:11:23.990
As a handicap for the engine
displacement difference,

00:11:23.990 --> 00:11:26.540
Raimu-senpai will start
thirty seconds after you.

00:11:26.540 --> 00:11:28.870
I don't care about the rules.

00:11:28.870 --> 00:11:31.080
This race is already over.

00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:34.750
Love shall win!

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:37.000
That's a lot of exhaust vapor.

00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:40.970
No wonder it was discontinued in a year.

00:11:40.970 --> 00:11:44.350
Three, two, one... Go!

00:11:47.720 --> 00:11:50.890
I have faith in you, Raimu-senpai.

00:11:50.890 --> 00:11:53.020
You promised to get rid of all

00:11:53.020 --> 00:11:55.650
the guys who come after me.

00:11:58.030 --> 00:11:59.900
You seem relaxed, Tazuko.

00:11:59.900 --> 00:12:03.110
Of course. Senpai always wins.

00:12:03.110 --> 00:12:05.280
True.

00:12:05.280 --> 00:12:09.910
You sure do trust Senpai, Tazuko.

00:12:09.910 --> 00:12:12.710
Hey! They're littering cigarette butts!

00:12:13.080 --> 00:12:14.210
I have to lecture them.

00:12:19.170 --> 00:12:21.130
Shit, shit, shit!

00:12:21.130 --> 00:12:23.840
What is this? I've never felt
so intimidated before!

00:12:42.490 --> 00:12:45.490
Yes! Yes! I finally got a girlfriend!

00:12:45.490 --> 00:12:47.160
I gotta tell mom!

00:12:47.570 --> 00:12:49.910
Come on, kiss me right now.

00:12:53.620 --> 00:12:55.000
Idiot!

00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:56.380
MVX!
Idiot!

00:12:56.380 --> 00:12:57.290
MVX!

00:12:57.670 --> 00:13:02.420
Raimu-senpai has always protected us.

00:13:02.420 --> 00:13:03.970
And even now...

00:13:03.970 --> 00:13:04.760
Huh?

00:13:04.760 --> 00:13:07.390
Senpai's still there, isn't she?

00:13:07.390 --> 00:13:09.220
How did you know?

00:13:09.220 --> 00:13:12.100
I get New Year's postcards every year

00:13:12.100 --> 00:13:14.020
from the Bike Club room address.

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:16.190
<b>Nakano</b>

00:13:16.190 --> 00:13:20.570
I wonder how long Raimu-senpai
has been there, though.
<b>Nakano</b>

00:13:20.860 --> 00:13:23.280
And I wonder how long she'll stay.

00:13:24.450 --> 00:13:28.280
There must be a reason she can't leave.

00:13:28.280 --> 00:13:32.700
How many students has she seen graduate now?

00:13:32.700 --> 00:13:36.870
I wonder if Senpai's ever going to graduate.

00:13:36.870 --> 00:13:38.290
You do burnouts

00:13:49.850 --> 00:13:51.220
like this.

00:13:51.220 --> 00:13:53.270
That's impossible for me to do!

00:13:53.270 --> 00:13:54.680
Don't give up!

00:13:54.680 --> 00:13:57.600
Senpai has to see how much we've grown!

00:13:57.600 --> 00:14:00.770
But is this really going to prove anything?

00:14:00.770 --> 00:14:02.480
Of course!

00:14:02.480 --> 00:14:05.240
By the time she graduates, we'll
learn how to write words with our bikes!

00:14:05.240 --> 00:14:09.410
And we'll leave the message for the school
to know that the bike club was here.

00:14:14.240 --> 00:14:15.500
Raimu-senpai.

00:14:17.500 --> 00:14:19.460
<b>Repeating the year</b>

00:14:19.460 --> 00:14:19.790
<b>Repeating the year</b>

00:14:19.790 --> 00:14:21.460
R-Repeating the year?
<b>Repeating the year</b>

00:14:21.460 --> 00:14:21.630
R-Repeating the year?

00:14:21.630 --> 00:14:24.340
So you'll be here next year?

00:14:28.130 --> 00:14:29.930
Ba
kuon<i>!!</i>

00:14:32.300 --> 00:14:33.890
Ba
kuon<i>!!</i>

00:14:38.020 --> 00:14:40.100
It's like a tunnel of cherry blossoms!

00:14:40.600 --> 00:14:42.270
Yahooi!!

00:14:44.530 --> 00:14:46.440
Yume!

00:14:48.780 --> 00:14:49.820
Onee-chan.

00:14:49.820 --> 00:14:51.410
Catch ya later!

00:14:52.160 --> 00:14:54.990
The Honda CV-400, "Super Four."

00:14:54.990 --> 00:14:56.830
You sure do know a lot.

00:14:56.830 --> 00:14:59.540
To me they all look the same.

00:14:59.540 --> 00:15:02.330
They're often used at driving schools.

00:15:02.330 --> 00:15:04.420
The seat is 755mm high.
TL Note: 30 inches

00:15:04.420 --> 00:15:04.500
TL Note: 30 inches

00:15:05.300 --> 00:15:08.760
Suzuki GSX 400S, "Katana."

00:15:08.760 --> 00:15:08.840
Seat height, 750mm.

00:15:08.840 --> 00:15:11.220
TL Note: 29 inches
Seat height, 750mm.

00:15:11.220 --> 00:15:11.930
Seat height, 750mm.

00:15:11.930 --> 00:15:14.140
Yamaha Serow, 225.

00:15:14.140 --> 00:15:14.220
A lower seat height for an off-roader, 810mm.

00:15:14.220 --> 00:15:17.310
TL Note: 32 inches
A lower seat height for an off-roader, 810mm.

00:15:17.310 --> 00:15:17.390
TL Note: 32 inches

00:15:18.520 --> 00:15:18.600
790mm.

00:15:18.600 --> 00:15:20.060
TL Note: 31 inches
790mm.

00:15:20.060 --> 00:15:20.640
790mm.

00:15:21.020 --> 00:15:24.980
Hey Chisame-chan, why do
you only remember the seat height?

00:15:24.980 --> 00:15:28.610
The center of gravity is the
most important thing when riding.

00:15:28.610 --> 00:15:30.820
In other words, the seat height.

00:15:31.990 --> 00:15:34.620
Everyone, please study, enjoy your clubs,

00:15:34.620 --> 00:15:37.040
